{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>וַיִּפֶן וַיֵּצֵא</b> — He treated him contemptibly in his eyes, for after he had confessed and said ״HaShem is the righteous one״ and so on, yet reverted to his foulness — therefore he turned and went out in the manner customary with the rest of men. And you will find that Pharaoh the wicked paid him back accordingly, as it is written ״וַיּוּשַׁב״ and so on, ״וַיְגָרֶשׁ אֹתָם מֵאֵת פְּנֵי פַרְעֹה״ (Exodus 10:8, 11). And therefore you will find that after this, when he called him to pray for the removal of the plague of locusts, he said to them ״חָטָאתִי לַה׳ וְלָכֶם״ (Exodus 10:16) — what he was not accustomed to say before — intending to confess for having conducted himself toward them with contempt and having driven them out."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:16.268100389Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}